  "aggregation_rules": {
    "legal": [
      "Within formal-v2.1, report the nine paired complete-OOF estimates and hierarchical paired bootstrap while retaining the 111-cat internal-validation boundary.",
      "Within each C1 round, use equal-weight base_seed-by-repeat estimates defined by that locked protocol and paired C1-minus-A0 differences.",
      "Across C1 rounds, report only a clearly labelled descriptive weighted mean and sign inventory because the role bank, cats, calls and metric are shared.",
      "Report CatMeows and dog results in separate task-specific tables with their own units, classes and baselines."
    ],
    "illegal": [
      "Treat seed-repeat cells, folds or repeated animal occurrences as independent animals.",
      "Combine pilot, formal and deterministic replication as independent studies without accounting for the same 111 cats.",
      "Pool formal complete outer-test OOF results with later inner-validation screens as if they were the same evaluation level.",
      "Pool CatMeows context Macro-F1, dog five-class age Macro-F1 and MeowAgeNet three-class age Macro-F1 into one effect estimate.",
      "Use CatMeows or dog-above-dummy results to rescue a failed MeowAgeNet adapter/C1 mechanism gate.",
      "Upgrade any IDEA077-082 module by selecting favorable seeds, splits, secondary metrics or post-outcome feature groups."
    ]
  },
